 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Standard and tolerance",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The element follows the DIN EN 60751 platinum characteristic. Each resistance value is made in two classes, F 0.3 (B) and the wider F 0.6 (2B); both apply over -50 °C to +130 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Upper temperature",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The rated range ends at +130 °C. Mounted on board material whose thermal expansion is matched to the chip, it can be used up to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Measuring current and self-heating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Pt100 parts are read with 0.3 to 1 mA and Pt1000 parts with 0.1 to 0.3 mA. At 0 °C the element warms by 0.8 K for every milliwatt dissipated in it, and this has to be taken into account."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Long-term stability",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Stored in air for 1000 hours at the top of its declared range, R(0 °C) moves by no more than the tolerance of its class under DIN EN 60751. A typical shift after 1000 hours at +150 °C is 0.06 %."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Pt1000 elements in 0603, 0805 and 1206 were reflowed in nitrogen and in air on a Benchmarker II test board with four surface finishes, using SnAgCu paste and a long High and a short Low limit profile, at three board positions (center, mass, mix). The parts mount face up and take reflow or wave soldering, for example double wave for no more than 8 s at 235 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Automotive use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part may also be used in automotive applications; on request YAGEO Nexensos assesses whether further requirements, for example IMDS or PPAP, can be met."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Compliance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "RoHS compliant. The part contains nickel, which falls under a California Proposition 65 warning."
  }
 ],
